  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The coordinates of \\(\\bigtriangleup ABC\\) are \\(A(5, 7),\\) \\(B(11, 7),\\) and \\(C(3, y),\\) with \\(y > 7.\\) The area of \\(\\bigtriangleup ABC\\) is \\(12.\\) What is the value of \\(y?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(8\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(9\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(11\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(12\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": "11"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2024-p11.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Consider the base of the triangle to be \\(\\overline{\\rm AB}\\) which has length \\(11-5=6\\). Given that the area of the triangle is \\(12\\), its height must be of length \\(\\dfrac{2(12)}{6}=4\\). Since \\(y>7\\), then \\(y\\) must be \\(7+4=11\\).\n\nThus, D is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Use \\(AB\\) as the base of the triangle",
        "The height from \\(C\\) to \\(AB\\) is \\(y-7\\)"
      ],
